# Local overrides — copy to .env.local. .env.local is gitignored and never committed.
#
# IMPORTANT: the two collector keys below do NOT work from this file.
# The stats collectors run as node child processes (vite.config.js statsPlugin
# → spawnSync, no `env` option) and read process.env directly. Vite does not
# write .env values into process.env, and dotenv is not a dependency of this
# repo, so a value set here reaches neither the dev-server collector nor a
# standalone `pnpm validate:epic-docs`. The latter skips silently while
# printing "This is NOT a pass".
#
# Verified 2026-08-06 by three runs (dummy key present, then file deleted,
# identical live fetches). See docs/backlog/SUG-268-governance-data-layer.md
# §Local environment hazard.
#
# Export them from your shell instead. Prefer ~/.zshenv over ~/.zshrc: zsh
# sources .zshrc for interactive shells only, and husky pre-commit hooks are
# not interactive.
#
#   export LINEAR_API_KEY="..."
#     Linear read-only personal token, scoped to Issues. Without it,
#     stats.linearRoadmap uses cached data from the last CI run, and
#     validate:epic-docs checks nothing.
#     Get one at: https://linear.app/settings/api → Personal API keys
#
#   export GITHUB_TOKEN="..."
#     GitHub personal token, public_repo scope. Without it, stats.github
#     uses cached data.
#
# VITE_* variables DO work from a file: those reach client code through
# import.meta.env. The distinction is node-side vs client-side, not the
# filename. Add any VITE_* overrides below.
